DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This links a new name in the specified directory to an existing file.

     Its arguments are:

     _d_v_p       The vnode of the directory.

     _v_p        The vnode of the file to be linked.

     _c_n_p       Pathname information about the file.

     The pathname info should _n_o_t be released on exit because it is done by
     the caller.  The directory and file vnodes should _n_o_t be released on
     exit.

LLOOCCKKSS
     VVOOPP__LLIINNKK() expects the directory and file vnodes to be locked on entry
     and will leave the vnodes locked on return.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Zero is returned if the file was linked successfully, otherwise an error
     is returned.

EERRRROORRSS
     [EMLINK]           The file has too many links.

     [EPERM]            The file is immutable.

     [EXDEV]            A hard link is not possible between different file
                        systems.

